  "title": "InwardScreen stock check failure allows 'Submit Anyway' bypass to submit unverified stock",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: business_logic. Severity: P1. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. When the pre-submission stock level check API call fails (network error, timeout, server error), the catch block presents an Alert with a 'Submit Anyway' button that calls doSubmit() directly, bypassing stock verification entirely. This means a retailer on a flaky connection can submit stock inward transactions without the server ever validating current levels, potentially creating phantom inventory or double-counting stock.",
